{"id": "EUVD-2026-80301", "enisaUuid": "b8f38329-5343-3176-9085-f297bd1bd823", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: qualcomm: rmnet: restore skb->dev on deaggregated frames\n\nrmnet_map_deaggregate() allocates each sub-frame with alloc_skb() and\nleaves skb->dev NULL. __rmnet_map_ingress_handler() assigns\nskb->dev = ep->egress_dev only on the data path, but a MAP command frame\nis dispatched to rmnet_map_command() before that, so rmnet_map_send_ack()\nruns netif_tx_lock(skb->dev) on a NULL device. An unprivileged user\nreaches this by unsharing a user+net namespace, creating an rmnet link\nover a tap device with INGRESS_DEAGGREGATION and INGRESS_MAP_COMMANDS,\nand writing an aggregated frame carrying a flow-control command to the\ntap fd.\n\nRestore the assignment dropped by 378e25357ac7, so every skb leaving\nrmnet_map_deaggregate() has a valid device.\n\n  BUG: KASAN: null-ptr-deref in _raw_spin_lock (kernel/locking/spinlock.c:158)\n  Write of size 4 at addr 00000000000004b4 by task exploit/144\n  Call Trace:\n   _raw_spin_lock (kernel/locking/spinlock.c:158)\n   netif_tx_lock (net/sched/sch_generic.c:497)\n   rmnet_map_command (drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/rmnet/rmnet_map_command.c:67)\n   rmnet_rx_handler (drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/rmnet/rmnet_handlers.c:125)\n   __netif_receive_skb_core.constprop.0 (net/core/dev.c:6103)\n   ...\n   __netif_receive_skb_one_core (net/core/dev.c:6214)\n   netif_receive_skb (net/core/dev.c:6474)\n   tun_get_user (drivers/net/tun.c:1966)\n   tun_chr_write_iter (drivers/net/tun.c:2012)\n   vfs_write (fs/read_write.c:687)\n   ksys_write (fs/read_write.c:739)\n   do_syscall_64 (arch/x86/entry/syscall_64.c:94)\n   entry_SYSCALL_64_after_hwframe (arch/x86/entry/entry_64.S:121)\n  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception in interrupt", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T08:48:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:52:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5aaa7409c1b4ca4c60d66e2afa99703bf4eb7ddd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b78ab84ddf97c06a8567edb62b6c0fd582f9a62", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d18c6c6cd1666b2cb7915cad052e22abf520997", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4bcef54e4a3355a62d9ad90729fe563435ec76c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b14c22c31d9e30f38ea1693ac06d318f32258f5d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7abe769e72c792e5f9eb273813eb3ecd8389854c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/200460a0793dc6af97d3b36d92ac245350ac26fc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a66734a1c5e36525ea07e9f4547fddc51e916de3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2f6m-7f8f-p7hp", "CVE-2026-89780"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "25cd5130-cedf-32dc-a1e4-b5d3ce936280", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "37e57281-a110-37b9-bb52-b95a0e86fe2b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.17"}, {"id": "44443f86-c030-3826-a413-3556628ea5ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "46b062b0-3246-33b6-9ef0-7ea1de5bdd69", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "4965649b-44fb-36f9-9230-70d52e07ce6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "378e25357ac78ad02fbc98bec9b4e3baaa916c5c <b14c22c31d9e30f38ea1693ac06d318f32258f5d"}, {"id": "4b26fe66-8beb-38b7-9680-4a74713dc625", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "4c437205-0da4-34d3-8ed9-ecb9c4b229a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "4eaa6c43-eecc-3d83-b942-5fbfc5ba7eba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "378e25357ac78ad02fbc98bec9b4e3baaa916c5c <7abe769e72c792e5f9eb273813eb3ecd8389854c"}, {"id": "611e872d-5c00-38aa-ae3d-fbc8